The service guides homeowners through a three-step process: submitting property details, providing energy usage data, and receiving a customized savings estimate. The platform identifies applicable state and federal incentives and matches users with local installers.

The primary audience is residential property owners in New Jersey seeking to evaluate solar adoption.

The company emphasizes a streamlined, no-obligation estimate process as its core value proposition.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar savings estimation", "Incentive qualification analysis", "Installer referral matching"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Three-step online savings estimate process", "Instant incentive qualification analysis", "Referral network of local solar installers"], "facts_used": ["Company name, headquarters city/state, website -> db", "Service description and three-step process -> page:/", "Phone number  -> page:/ (excluded from profile)"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "This allows us to find the best solar installers in your area as well as the best incentives and credits that you qualify for.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='new-jersey-solar-initiative' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Located in Albuquerque, New Mexico, New Mexico Diesel Power Inc. is an automotive repair shop owned and operated by Jimmy Ball. The business has been serving the area for decades, with a team that brings over 50 years of combined experience. Ball took over ownership in January of an unspecified year, continuing a legacy of diesel-focused repair.

The shop provides complete automotive repair for all makes and models except European vehicles, with a specialization in diesel engines. Services include computer diagnostics, oil changes, scheduled maintenance, and pre-purchase and post-purchase vehicle inspections. A team of three ASE-certified technicians — Jimmy, Brandon, and Andrew — perform bumper-to-bumper repairs, including electrical and computer diagnostics, using OEM parts whenever possible.

The technicians hold Ford certifications, including one Triple Master Technician credential from 2006, allowing the shop to serve as an alternative to dealership service departments.

