service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Complete Automotive Repair on all makes and models except European vehicles.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='new-mexico-diesel-power-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='New Mexico Manufacturing Extension Partnership (New Mexico MEP) operates from Albuquerque, New Mexico. As the official representative of the MEP National Network in the state, it functions as a NIST MEP approved center. The organization is structured as a public-private partnership that brings together government, not-for-profit, and industry resources.

The center delivers advisory and technical services to small and mid-sized manufacturers. Its offerings include process optimization, product development, scale-up processes, lean methodologies, workforce development, growth services, efficiency improvements, quality management systems, manufacturing safety, supply chain assistance, and connection to resources. Services are provided at reduced cost through a network of resource partners.

Clients span various manufacturing sectors in New Mexico. Examples include Old Barrel Tea Company in Albuquerque, which reported a 30% increase in online sales; Los Poblanos in Los Ranchos, which saw improved output and cycle time; Wicked Edge, a precision knife-sharpening equipment maker serving law enforcement and outdoor markets; and Navajo Spirit in Gallup, producing traditional-inspired clothing. The center also collaborates with companies such as TEAM Technologies, Alaska Structures, Valencia Flour Mill, Insight Lighting, OBG Architectural Millwork, and Santa Fe Spirits.

New Mexico MEP distinguishes itself through its affiliation with the MEP National Network, which the W.E. Upjohn Institute found delivered a 13.6-to-1 return on investment in 2020. The center emphasizes hands-on assistance and technology-driven solutions to help manufacturers overcome growth barriers.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Process optimization", "Product development", "Scale-up processes", "Lean methodologies", "Workforce development", "Growth services", "Efficiency improvements", "Quality management systems", "Manufacturing safety", "Supply chain assistance", "Resource connections"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["NIST MEP approved Center and official state representative of the MEP National Network", "Public-private partnership leveraging government, non-profit, and industry resources", "Services offered at minimal cost through resource partner network", "Hands-on, technology-driven assistance for small and mid-sized manufacturers"], "facts_used": ["Location: Albuquerque, New Mexico -> db", "NIST MEP approved Center, official representative of MEP National Network -> /", "Public-private partnership bringing government, non-profit, industry resources -> /about-us", "Services: process optimization, product development, scale-up, lean, workforce development, growth services, efficiency, quality management, safety, supply chain, connections -> /", "Services offered at minimal cost through resource partners -> /about-us", "Client examples: Old Barrel Tea Company, Los Poblanos, Wicked Edge, Navajo Spirit, TEAM Technologies, Alaska Structures, Valencia Flour Mill, Insight Lighting, OBG Architectural Millwork, Santa Fe Spirits -> /about-us", "MEP program 13.6:1 ROI in 2020 per W.E. Upjohn Institute -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "As a NIST MEP approved Center, New Mexico M.E.P. is the official representative of the MEP National Network in our state.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='new-mexico-manufacturing-extension-partnership-new-mexico-mep' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='New Mexico School Products was founded in 1968 in Albuquerque, New Mexico. The company began as a full-coverage furniture provider for educational, government, and private institutional markets.

In 1986, the company established its own manufacturing plant, FAME Mfg., enabling in-house production of a customizable furniture line. Today, New Mexico School Products designs, builds, supplies, and installs furniture for classrooms, libraries, gymnasiums, cafeterias, and theaters. It combines its FAME product line with offerings from manufacturing partners to deliver both off-the-shelf and custom solutions. The operation includes complimentary on-site space planning using client blueprints and free ergonomic assessments for teachers and administrators.

The company serves educational institutions, government agencies, and private organizations across the United States. Projects have included schools, libraries, gymnasiums, cafeterias, and theaters. It also supplies automotive parts storage units, indicating a presence in the industrial storage market.

New Mexico School Products emphasizes quality through FAME Manufacturing’s participation in the Architectural Woodwork Institute (AWI) and Quality Certification Program (QCP). Its differentiators include complimentary space planning, ergonomic assessments, a customizable in-house product line, and a network of manufacturing partners, all backed by over 50 years of experience.', certifications=ARRAY['AWI participant','QCP participant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Space planning", "Ergonomic assessments", "Custom furniture design", "Furniture manufacturing", "Furniture installation", "Furniture procurement", "Library furnishing", "Gymnasium furnishing", "Classroom layout design", "Seating solutions", "Storage solutions"], "industries": ["Education", "Government", "Private organizations", "Automotive Parts Units", "AUTOMOTIVE PARTS STORAGE UNITS"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Complimentary on-site space planning using client blueprints", "Free ergonomic assessments for teachers and administrators", "FAME Manufacturing participates in AWI and QCP quality programs", "Customizable FAME product line manufactured in-house since 1986", "Premier manufacturing partnerships for off-the-shelf solutions"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1968 -> /about-us", "Started manufacturing plant FAME Mfg in 1986 -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Albuquerque, New Mexico -> db", "Offers free space planning and ergonomic assessments -> /", "Serves educational, government, private organizations -> /about-us", "FAME Manufacturing is an AWI and QCP participant -> /about-us", "Provides custom furniture solutions for schools, libraries, gyms, cafeterias, theaters -> /about-us", "Offers library and gym furnishings -> /", "Automotive parts storage units product line -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "New Mexico School Products took the initiative in 1986 to start its own manufacturing plant, FAME Mfg.", "founded_year": "1968", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='new-mexico-school-products' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='New Tech Metals operates from New Franken, Wisconsin, where it was founded in 1982 as New Tech Metalworks. The company is a veteran-owned, family-owned small business. Ownership passed to the Blackman family in 2003 when brothers Jeff, Keith, and David Blackman acquired the shop. Today, the second generation — Adam and Andy Blackman, both U.S. Army veterans, and their cousin Derek Blackman — own and run the operation. Adam served as a 19D Cavalry Scout and Andy as a 19K M1 Armor Crewman, experience they say informs the discipline applied to every part.

The shop provides six in-house capabilities: design and development, cutting (laser, turret punch, plasma), forming (press brakes), welding (AWS-certified across nine codes), CNC machining (milling and turning), and assembly with finishing. Equipment includes a 5-ton overhead crane, Mitsubishi fiber lasers, Strippit turret, Safan Darley press brakes, Haas VMC and EC-500 machining centers, FANUC robotic welding cells, and Haeger/Timesavers finishing systems. The facility added a 7,000-square-foot office expansion in 2012 and maintains in-house material stock. Production focuses on low- to mid-volume, high-reliability components for defense and industrial OEMs.

New Tech Metals serves three core sectors. In defense, it supplies Tier-2 components to OEMs and prime contractors for over 20 vehicle platforms, shipboard infrastructure, weapons support equipment, communications enclosures, and structural assemblies. Transportation customers include fire apparatus, refuse vehicles, concrete mixers, cargo trailers, airport ground-support equipment, and automotive programs. For machine and equipment builders, the shop produces parts for packaging equipment, paper converting, drying and curing systems, commercial appliances, power equipment, and material handling systems.

The company emphasizes that its veteran ownership brings a culture of accountability and precision that goes beyond standard quality certifications. It operates under a single ITAR-registered roof with DFARS material compliance, NIST/CMMC cybersecurity controls, and ISO 9001:2015 quality management. The owners quote jobs directly and remain accountable through delivery, offering one quote, one schedule, and one team from print to packout.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ITAR Compliant','AS9100','AWS Certified Welders (D1.1, D1.2, D1.3, D1.6, D9.1, D17.1)','NIST & CMMC Cybersecurity Compliant','DFARS Material Compliant','DDTC Registered','SAM Registered','SBA Certified Veteran-Owned Small Business (VOSB)','Six Sigma Green Belt Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design & Development (DFM Review, Prototyping, Value Engineering)", "Laser Cutting (Mitsubishi ML3015 eX-F60-D fiber laser)", "Turret Punching (Strippit Turret)", "Plasma Cutting", "Press Brake Forming (Safan Darley, E-Brake)", "Welding (TIG, MIG, FANUC Robotic, AWS D1.1, D1.2, D1.3, D1.6, D9.1, D17.1)", "CNC Machining (Milling, Turning, Haas VMC, Haas EC-500)", "Assembly & Finishing (Haeger 824, Timesavers, Pemsertion)", "In-House Material Stock", "5-Ton Overhead Crane", "Shipping & Receiving"], "industries": ["Defense", "Transportation", "Machine & Equipment Builders"], "materials": ["Carbon steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum alloys", "Copper", "Brass", "Exotics"], "equipment": ["Strippit Turret", "Mitsubishi ML3015 eX-F60-D fiber laser", "Plasma cutting system", "Safan Darley Press Brake", "E-Brake", "Haas VMC", "Haas EC-500", "CNC Mill", "Haeger 824", "Timesavers", "Pemsertion", "FANUC Robotic Welding", "5-Ton Overhead Crane", "SmartFlex Rapid Tower Automation"], "volume": "Low to mid-volume high reliability components; prototype through production", "lead_time": "6 to 10 weeks for first-article defense parts", "tolerances": "\u00b10.0005\"", "built_on": ["All six fabrication capabilities in-house under one ITAR-registered roof", "AWS-certified welders across nine welding codes (D1.1, D1.2, D1.3, D1.6, D9.1, D17.1)", "Veteran-owned, family-owned small business with direct owner accountability", "DFARS material compliant and NIST/CMMC cybersecurity compliant", "Prototype to production CNC machining holding \u00b10.0005\" tolerance"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 as New Tech Metalworks -> /about-us", "Veteran-owned, family-owned small business -> /, /about-us", "Blackman family ownership (Jeff, Keith, David 2003; Adam, Andy, Derek second generation) -> /about-us", "Adam Blackman 19D Cavalry Scout, Andy Blackman 19K M1 Armor Crewman -> /about-us", "Six in-house capabilities: design, cutting, forming, welding, machining, assembly -> /, /services", "Equipment list (Mitsubishi laser, Strippit turret, Safan Darley press brakes, Haas VMC/EC-500, FANUC robotic welding, Haeger 824, Timesavers, Pemsertion, 5-ton crane) -> /services", "7,000 sq ft office expansion 2012 -> /about-us", "Low to mid-volume high reliability components for defense -> /", "Defense applications: 20+ vehicle platforms, shipboard infrastructure, weapons support, communications enclosures, structural assemblies -> /", "Transportation: fire apparatus, refuse vehicles, concrete mixers, cargo trailers, airport ground-support, automotive -> /", "Machine & Equipment: packaging, paper converting, drying/curing, commercial appliance, power equipment, material handling -> /", "ITAR registered, DDTC registered, DFARS compliant, NIST/CMMC compliant, ISO 9001:2015 -> /, /about-us", "AWS certified welders across nine codes -> /services", "\u00b10.0005\" tolerance -> /services", "First-article defense parts 6-10 weeks -> / (insights)", "CAGE code 5VUL8 -> /about-us", "SBA VOSB certification 2026 -> /about-us", "Materials: carbon, stainless, aluminum, copper, brass, exotics -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Development, machining, forming, welding, and finishing, all under one roof in New Franken. Real capacity, real equipment, real steel moving every shift.", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "5VUL8", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered", "DDTC Registered", "DFARS Material Compliant"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned", "Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='new-tech-metals' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='New York Parts Specialists Inc operates from Long Island City, New York. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed. It does business as NY Parts, focusing on supplying authentic industrial bearings and related components.

The company distributes a range of industrial products including bearings and accessories, relays, contactors, tachometers, motors and motor controls, sensors, and seals. It carries established brands such as SKF, NTN, INA (Schaeffler), and ABB. The business model centers on distribution rather than manufacturing, offering custom quotes for large industrial and OEM orders.

NY Parts serves customers in renewable energy and energy efficiency sectors, as well as broader industrial and OEM markets. The company highlights its ability to support large-scale orders with custom quoting and emphasizes fast, trackable delivery with easy returns.

