UPDATE companies SET description='Nomad Furniture operates from Farr West, Utah, where the Mitchell family relocated the business in 2019 after purchasing it from Albuquerque bed maker Dave Cady. Cady had built the brand over more than 30 years in New Mexico before retiring. Connor Mitchell, joined by his parents Ken and Ana, trained with Cady and moved the operation to northern Utah, establishing a family-owned shop where every member contributes.

The company handcrafts platform beds and nightstands from solid North American hardwoods — oak, maple, and other species — using zero-VOC finishes such as Daddy Van’s all-natural hemp oil and Rubio products. Each piece is designed and built in their Utah workshop, featuring upgraded premium rails, slats, and a center leg for added strength. No veneers, particleboard, or upcycled woods are used.

Nomad Furniture sells directly to residential customers seeking durable, non-toxic bedroom furniture. Reviews highlight buyers who appreciate the solid construction, easy assembly, and healthy finishes, with one customer noting the bed handled a heavy latex mattress without issue. The company ships free anywhere in the continental United States.

After a devastating shop fire in June 2024 destroyed all equipment and materials, the Mitchells rebuilt with the help of son-in-law Jake, an engineer. The recovery led to refined designs and a renewed commitment to zero-VOC materials, positioning the company around resilience, American craftsmanship, and a healthier home environment.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Handcrafted woodworking", "Zero-VOC finishing", "Furniture design", "Solid hardwood fabrication", "Assembly and shipping"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Bedroom furniture", "Home furnishings"], "materials": ["North American hardwoods (oak, maple)", "Zero-VOC finishes (Daddy Van''s hemp oil, Rubio)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Zero-VOC finishes (hemp oil and Rubio)", "Handcrafted from solid North American hardwoods with no veneers or particleboard", "Upgraded premium rails, slats, and center leg for structural strength", "Free shipping anywhere in the continental U.S.", "Family-owned and operated in Utah"], "facts_used": ["Mitchell family purchased Nomad Furniture in summer 2019 from Dave Cady -> /about-us", "Business originally built by Dave Cady over 30 years in Albuquerque -> /about-us", "Relocated to Farr West, Utah -> /about-us", "Shop fire in June 2024 destroyed equipment and materials -> /about-us", "Rebuilt with son-in-law Jake, engineer -> /about-us", "Upgraded premium rails, slats, center leg -> /about-us", "Switched to Daddy Van''s hemp oil and Rubio finishes, zero-VOC -> /about-us", "Handcrafted from solid North American hardwoods, no veneers/particleboard -> /about-us, /", "Platform beds: Pecos, Sedona, Mesa, Santa Cruz -> /", "Nightstand introduced after fire -> /about-us", "Free shipping in continental US -> /", "Customer reviews mention 4-week delivery, easy assembly -> /", "Family-owned, all members contribute -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Ogden, Utah per database -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Each bed is hand-built from locally sourced American hardwoods.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='nomad-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Nordic Semiconductor, Inc. operates from Portland, Oregon, where it develops ultra-low-power wireless semiconductors and cloud services for the Internet of Things. The company does not disclose its founding year or ownership structure in public materials.

The firm designs and supplies system-on-chips (SoCs), system-in-packages (SiPs), and pre-certified modules — including the nRF54L series, the dual-core nRF5340, and the nRF93M1 Cat 1 bis cellular modem — alongside the nPM1300 power management IC. Its nRF Cloud platform, built on Memfault technology, provides chip-to-cloud device management, embedded observability, location services, and lifetime flat-rate FOTA updates. The latest nRF54LM20B integrates an Axon neural processing unit for on-device machine learning.

Nordic’s components appear in consumer, healthcare, industrial, and educational devices. The BBC micro:bit, now in its tenth year with Nordic silicon, has reached 73 million students worldwide. Other deployments include See.Sense’s NB-IoT cycle tracker, MEZOO’s remote cardiac monitoring system, Polar’s multisport watches, Lynxemi’s industrial asset-health sensors, Bettear’s Auracast audio streamers, eCozy’s Matter-enabled smart thermostats, and the IDR01 smart ring.

