UPDATE companies SET description='North Star Systems, Inc. was founded in 1997 in Pelham, Alabama, by the former management team of SRT Electro-Optics, Inc., a subsidiary of Southern Research. The small business operates from the Birmingham area and was established to serve commercial, industrial, and defense clients with engineering and production services.

The company provides electronic circuit design, embedded software development, electro-optics, servo controls, and video signal processing. Its capabilities span prototype hardware development, transition-to-production, production test equipment design, quality assurance documentation, and configuration management. North Star has delivered projects ranging from video recording equipment controllers and infrared target collection systems to remote weapon stations, gun control units, and airborne fire-retardant dispensing controls.

Customers include U.S. Army programs such as the Integrated Sensor Architecture, missile and ground vehicle platforms, naval vessels, and aircraft systems. The firm also serves the nuclear power sector (independent verification and validation), commercial video recording and editing equipment manufacturers, welding machine tool builders, and firefighting air-tanker operators. Work has covered DISA STIG compliance, MISB metadata standards, and electromagnetic compatibility testing.

North Star emphasizes its 30-plus years of aerospace and defense experience and its ability to redesign products for parts obsolescence while adding new features. The team focuses on solving challenging problems to make customers successful, offering a responsive, experienced crew that can take a concept through live-fire testing and full-rate production.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electronic circuit design", "Embedded system software development", "Electro-optics engineering", "Servo controls design", "Video signal processing", "Independent verification and validation (IV&V)", "Prototype hardware development", "Transition-to-production management", "Production test equipment development", "Quality assurance documentation", "Configuration management", "Parts obsolescence redesign", "Wireless data link design (RF 900MHz, 2.5GHz)", "Fiber-optic video/communications links", "Gimbal design", "Line-of-sight stabilization", "Video target detection and tracking", "Laser rangefinder integration", "Marinization (marine environment component selection)", "Ballistic algorithm development", "Remote weapon systems integration", "Gun control unit development", "Digital data recorder design", "Fire retardant dispensing system controls"], "industries": ["Aerospace and Defense", "Nuclear Power Generation", "Industrial Controls", "Commercial Video Recording and Editing", "Welding Industry", "Firefighting (Air-Tanker)", "Commercial RF Communications", "Defense System LRUs"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["30+ years of aerospace and defense engineering experience", "Transition-to-production expertise for defense and commercial hardware", "Redesign and reengineering for parts obsolescence", "Small Business with responsive, experienced engineering team", "SBIR project experience (Infrared Target Collection System)"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1997 by former management team of SRT Electro-Optics, Inc. -> /about", "Headquartered in Pelham, Alabama (database) / Based in Birmingham, AL (page) -> db, /about", "Small Business designation -> /about", "Engineering capabilities: electronic circuit design, embedded software, electro-optics, servo controls, video signal processing -> /about", "Projects: video recording equipment controllers, IV&V for nuclear power, SBIR infrared target collection, airborne retardant dispensing controls, ultrasonic welding controls, image target tracking, remote weapon systems, high-speed telemetry recording -> /about", "Aerospace and defense experience >30 years; work on missiles, ground vehicles, ships, aircraft, test systems -> /about", "Specific defense standards: US Army ISA, DISA STIGs, MISB standards, EMC/EMI -> /about", "Industrial controls: video recorders, editing equipment, ultrasonic tools, TV cameras, wireless data links (900MHz/2.5GHz), solid-state data recorders -> /about", "Transition-to-production experience: remote weapon stations, commercial video equipment, welding machine tools, air-tanker controllers, airborne gimbals, video trackers, RF communications, fiber-optic data links -> /about", "Redesign for parts obsolescence example: Timing and Control Board for Esonix Ultrasonic Impact Generator, programmable flow controller -> /about", "Industries served: Defense System LRUs -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "to serve commercial, industrial, and defense clients; transition-to-production of the following: Remote Weapon Stations, Commercial Video Recording and Digital Editing Equipment", "founded_year": "1997", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='north-star-systems-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Northe Woodworking operates from an 8,500-square-foot workshop in Lewiston, Maine. The company began with a handful of tools and a commitment to traditional craftsmanship, but a fire at its original Mechanic Falls shop forced a restart after one year. That setback sharpened the team’s focus and deepened their dedication to building cabinetry that feels as though it has always belonged in a space.

The studio produces custom cabinetry, architectural millwork, built-in furniture, kitchens, and vanities, scaling from single pieces to full-home millwork packages. A full team of craftspeople works in the Lewiston facility, handling design, fabrication, and finishing for projects that range from traditional to contemporary styles.

Northe serves architects, interior designers, and homeowners throughout New England and the broader Northeast, including Maine, Massachusetts, New York, and Connecticut. Recent collaborations have included a Brooklyn brownstone renovation and a new coastal Maine build, illustrating the geographic reach of their client base.

